course: dictionary
lesson: 3021
title: Dynamo: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dynamo is a machine. It turns movement into electricity. «A bike dynamo spins a magnet in a coil and turns the movement of the wheel into electricity for the lamp.» The clue is the word movement: the wheel moves, and electricity comes out.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «She is a dynamo of energy» does not talk about a machine at all. Ask yourself: does the sentence describe a thing or a person? When a person is called a dynamo, the word means someone full of energy who gets lots done.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «A human dynamo» tells you it is a person, because human means a person. Then try your meaning in the sentence: "She is a person full of energy who gets lots done" makes sense, so you have worked it out.
explain: Dynamo is also part of the name of some sports clubs, such as Dynamo Kyiv. When a word is a name, you do not need its meaning to know what it is. A dictionary tells you when a word is a name.
fact: A dynamo is a machine that turns movement into electricity.
fact: «A dynamo of energy» means a person who is full of energy and gets lots done.
fact: «The Earth's magnetism comes from deep inside, where hot liquid iron swirls in the outer core like a giant dynamo.»
fact: A bike dynamo makes more electricity the faster the wheel spins.
fact: Dynamo is part of the names of some sports clubs, such as Dynamo Kyiv.
exercise: «A bike dynamo spins a magnet in a coil.» What does a bike dynamo make? | Water for the wheel | Sound for the bell | *Electricity for the lamp | Heat for the pedals
exercise: «She is a dynamo on the netball court, always busy and full of energy.» What does dynamo mean here? | *A person full of energy who gets lots done | A sleepy animal | A machine that makes electricity | A type of football club
exercise: Hannah says a dynamo is a loud noise. What is wrong with her idea? | It is a noise like thunder | It is always a person | Nothing, she is right | *It is a machine that makes electricity from movement, not a noise
test: «The Earth's magnetism comes from hot liquid iron swirling like a giant dynamo.» In this sentence, what is a dynamo like? | A loud singer | A football team that wins every match | A bike lamp | *A machine that turns movement into electricity
test: Tom says, «Ella is a dynamo!» What does he mean? | A machine in her bike | She is a football club | *She is full of energy and gets lots done | She is very sleepy
exam: Which sentence uses dynamo as a machine? | «He is a dynamo at school, always busy.» | *«A bike dynamo lights the lamp when the wheel turns.» | «She is a dynamo of energy.» | «Dynamo Kyiv played well on Saturday.»
